body:
So I did some research, and from my understanding the issue could be caused by subgroup clustering in the scene fragment shader:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7826b6b13fccf57d1461794afc560853c4d2531d/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl#L1464-L1476

Unfortunately, I don't understand enough about the inner workings here, but to me it looks like this gets somehow batched / split into groups of 32, and those groups are computed independently, ignoring sorting offsets from other "subgroups". Please note that this might not be the actual case, but rather it's my current understanding.

I did thorough debugging of the `TextureStorage::update_decal_buffer` method to see if the sorting is correct at this stage, and I can confirm that it works as expected.
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7826b6b13fccf57d1461794afc560853c4d2531d/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/texture_storage.cpp#L3090

I also prepared two visualizations of the scene shader, the first one shows that the `decal_index` is being calculated correctly (but the rendering is still incorrect, the black square should always be on top) :

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9035e5b5-4dd7-4fe8-a112-d41dacb2df4f

```glsl
if (decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect != vec4(0.0)) {
	//has albedo
	vec4 decal_albedo;
	if (sc_decal_use_mipmaps()) {
		decal_albedo = textureGrad(sampler2D(decal_atlas_srgb, decal_sampler), uv_local.xz * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw + decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.xy, ddx * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw, ddy * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw);
	} else {
		decal_albedo = textureLod(sampler2D(decal_atlas_srgb, decal_sampler), uv_local.xz * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw + decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.xy, 0.0);
	}
	decal_albedo *= decals.data[decal_index].modulate;
	decal_albedo.a *= fade;
	albedo = mix(albedo, decal_albedo.rgb, decal_albedo.a * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_mix);

  	frag_color = vec4(vec3(decal_index / 255.0), 1.0); // <----- Added debug color based on the decal_index
	return;
```
___
The second one shows that the issue could be caused by batching decals computations by groups of 32 here:
https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7826b6b13fccf57d1461794afc560853c4d2531d/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered.glsl#L1473-L1476

Video shows that the biggest decal is being processed in the second loop iteration when there are more than 32 decals:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0773781e-28a2-427c-bae8-7bf296834bcd

```glsl
if (decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect != vec4(0.0)) {
	//has albedo
	vec4 decal_albedo;
	if (sc_decal_use_mipmaps()) {
		decal_albedo = textureGrad(sampler2D(decal_atlas_srgb, decal_sampler), uv_local.xz * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw + decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.xy, ddx * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw, ddy * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw);
	} else {
		decal_albedo = textureLod(sampler2D(decal_atlas_srgb, decal_sampler), uv_local.xz * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.zw + decals.data[decal_index].albedo_rect.xy, 0.0);
	}
	decal_albedo *= decals.data[decal_index].modulate;
	decal_albedo.a *= fade;
	albedo = mix(albedo, decal_albedo.rgb, decal_albedo.a * decals.data[decal_index].albedo_mix);

  	frag_color = vec4(vec3(i * 64.0 / 255.0), 1.0);  // <----- Added debug color based on the loop index (multiplied by 64 for clarity)
	return;
```

Unfortunately, I don't think I can do much more here at this moment.
